e length, in tenths, of the dashes in a dashed line. Ignored if the corresponding line-type attribute is not dashed."}]}]},{"name":"spaceLength","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The length, in tenths, of the spaces in a dashed line. Ignored if the corresponding line-type attribute is not dashed."}]}]},{"name":"position","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways."}]}]},{"name":"font","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names.The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font."}]}]},{"name":"color","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}]}]},{"name":"bendSound","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The bend-sound type is used for bend and slide elements, and is similar to the trill-sound attribute group. Here the beats element refers to the number of discrete elements (like MIDI pitch bends) used to represent a continuous bend or slide. The first-beat indicates the percentage of the duration for starting a bend; the last-beat the percentage for ending it. The default choices are:"}]}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSlide"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSlide\/init(id:value:k